<?php

namespace Illuminate\Support;

/**
 * Empty re-declaration kept on purpose. Two reasons:
 *
 *  1. It DECLARES `Illuminate\Support\Arr` for projects whose analyzed vendor does not
 *     reflect `illuminate/support` (e.g. slim libraries like laravel/socialite). Without
 *     it every `Arr::` reference there becomes `UndefinedClass`.
 *  2. Laravel 13.18.0's reflected conditional `@return ($number is null ? mixed : array)` on
 *     `random()` was once dropped to `mixed` unless the class was re-declared here. On Psalm 7.2.1
 *     it resolves the same with or without this stub when `illuminate/support` is reflected, so
 *     reason 1 is what keeps the file.
 *
 * `random()` itself is intentionally NOT stubbed: the reflected conditional already resolves
 * literal, nullable and template-typed `$number`, and a stub conditional resolves identically
 * (probed on Psalm 7.2.1), so a stub would only duplicate it. The `Macroable` trait is copied
 * verbatim per stub convention; every static helper merges from reflection.
 */
class Arr
{
    use Traits\Macroable;
}
